<title>UK: Lonrho rises after Anglo raises stake.</title>
<headline>Lonrho rises after Anglo raises stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lonrho advanced 4-1/2 pence to 163-1/2 after South African mining giant Anglo American said it would raise its stake in the British conglomerate by 18.3 percent at 180 pence a share.</p>
<p>Anglo now holds 25.9 percent of Lonrho after the latter's chief executive Dieter Bock exercised his put option to sell his 18.3 percent holding to the South African firm.  </p>
<p>The option deal between Bock and Anglo was concluded in April.</p>
<p>The option's exercise comes nearly two weeks after a British newspaper reported that Anglo was no longer interested in raising its stake in Lonrho. The British conglomerate said at the time the Evening Standard report lacked foundation.</p>
